There is one aspect of projectile fighting that I really hate, and that
I WISH somebody would do something about (since it's more like a bug
than any intentional feature of the game.) It bugs me enough that,
though elven ranger is my favorite character, I ascended one and then
gave up on the class forever.

Suppose you're able to fire 4 arrows per round. Your first three arrows
happen to kill the creature you're fighting. Then the last one goes
flying on beyond its dead carcass, to: (pick one)

a) hit the opposite wall and fall to the floor uselessly.
b) land with a sploosh in a nearby moat or pool. Goodbye arrow.
c) hit a peaceful, who then becomes angry and attacks.
d) hit your pet, causing a rumble of distant thunder.
e) hit your Quest Leader. Big trouble.
f) and so on, and so on...

There should definitely be a "stop firing" option that players can set
in order to automatically STOP FIRING more ammo if the monster they're
trying to kill is dead! I'd write the patch myself, but unfortunately I
have absolutely no knowledge of how to do so. Anyone else out there
really annoyed at this problem?

